source	Thomas Aquinas, Summa Theologica I, tr. Fathers of the English Dominican Province (1920), q.2 a.3
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 17611, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/17611
class	inference
at	S4	Now the maximum in any genus is the cause of all in that genus
fault	from degrees of a quality to the existence of a maximum that causes the rest needs a Platonic premise the passage only illustrates (fire, the hottest, causes all heat)
reference	A. Kenny, The Five Ways (1969), ch. 5
